Clean. Here's what changed and why:

**New files:**
- `SimulationEvent.java` — immutable value object carrying `step`, `field`, and `nightTime`; decouples the payload from the source
- `SimulationObserver.java` — interface with `onStepCompleted(SimulationEvent)` + `isViable(Field)`

**`Simulator.java`:**
- Removed `private SimulatorView view`; replaced with `private final List<SimulationObserver> observers`
- Added `addObserver(SimulationObserver)` so any number of observers can be registered
- Constructor creates `SimulatorView` locally, configures colors, then calls `addObserver(view)` — `Simulator` never holds a typed `SimulatorView` reference after construction
- `simulateOneStep()` and `reset()` now call `notifyObservers(new SimulationEvent(...))` instead of `view.showStatus(...)`
- `simulate()` loop condition calls private `checkViable(field)` which delegates to all observers (halts if any returns false)

**`SimulatorView.java`:**
- Implements `SimulationObserver`
- Removed `private Simulator simulator` back-reference (was the circular dependency)
- Constructor no longer takes a `Simulator` argument
- `onStepCompleted` → calls `showStatus` with the event's data
- `showStatus` signature updated to `showStatus(int step, Field field, boolean nightTime)` — gets `nightTime` from the event instead of querying the simulator
- `isViable` already existed; now carries `@Override`

